{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of the heavens</b> etc. Since at first it was brief regarding some matters, now it goes back and explains how they were made. Rabbi Abba Hu said: every place where 'these' is said, it invalidates the preceding ones. Here it invalidates Tohu and Bohu and darkness." "<b>Generations of the heavens:</b> luminaries and stars and the subject of the Chariot, and the rest of the things above, such as fire, hail, snow, stormwind and tempest — except that David came and brought them down below to earth." "<b>And the earth:</b> living creatures, grasses, trees, stones, waters. <b>On the day of making:</b> on the day that heavens and earth were first made — these are the generations that He made afterward, each and every one in its time." "<b>On the day YHWH Elohim made:</b> now that heavens and earth were built in their fullness, He mentioned upon them the distinctive Name, because 'in the multitude of people is the majesty of the King,' and so we find that one does not recite [a blessing] over food with [the divine] Name with fewer than ten. Here Rashi explained that the Holy One, blessed be He, joined the attribute of mercy with the attribute of judgment, and that is what is written, 'וה׳ שמים עשה' — its meaning: He who is the master of the attribute of mercy, with His attribute of judgment, made the heavens." "<b>Earth and heavens,</b> whereas above it says 'et the heavens and et the earth.' In the Tanhuma they said: at creation, the heavens preceded the earth, but at fashioning and setting right, the earth preceded the heavens."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:25.025524681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}